  "# ADR-2607184800: Resolved-address pinning and unambiguous HTTP framing

**Status**: accepted
**Date**: 2026-07-18

## Decision

Production transport capability kits must scope both the requested hostname and
port and the canonical numeric addresses that DNS may resolve. The JVM provider
resolves once, selects only an allowed InetAddress, connects directly to that
address, and retains the original hostname for SNI and HTTPS endpoint identity.
This closes the pre-connect DNS-rebinding seam without granting ambient DNS
authority to the component.

The Kotoba HTTP provider compares Content-Length names ASCII-case-insensitively,
requires at most one such field, and rejects every Transfer-Encoding response.
Rejecting chunked framing is intentional until a bounded decoder has its own
conformance and adversarial evidence.

## Maturity boundary

This is a production admission rule and executable local negative evidence, not
full network qualification. IDNA normalization, IPv6 policy ergonomics,
external PKI/revocation, bounded chunked decoding, and protocol-specific DB
authentication and transactions remain open."}]
